.TH CHG 1 "October 2026"
.SH NAME
chg \- drive the media changer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chg
.BI load " set:vol onto drive"
.br
.B chg
.BI unload " drive"
.br
.B chg
.BI query " set|drive"
.br
.B chg
.BI next " drive"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I chg
writes its arguments as one command line to
.IR /dev/mediachg ,
the out-of-band media changer, and prints the one-line response.  It
exits 0 on
.B ok
and 1 on
.BR error .
The grammar is sys/MEDIACHG.md: a media set is a numbered list of
diskette images, a drive is
.IB djdma : n,
and volume numbers start at 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chg load dist8:0 onto djdma:0
chg query dist8          # ok 9
chg next djdma:0
chg unload djdma:0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
sys/MEDIACHG.md
